{
  "ruleId": "RATE-CG-COST-INFLATION-INDEX",
  "ruleSet": "RS-RATE-CG-COST-INFLATION-INDEX",
  "_note": "The Cost Inflation Index for each financial year, for the capital-gains measure only (W-088g, D-426; decided in W-088g1, D-424 C2a). Its one reader is the indexed-cost measure of long-term land or building (RS-CG-INDEXED-COST; 1961 s.48's second proviso and Explanation (iii); 2025 s.72(2) and (8)(b)-(c)). It is a second table rather than RATE-COST-INFLATION-INDEX widened, because that rule's reader, the accommodation cap (PERQ-ACCOM-CONTINUED), refuses a first year the table does not hold, and widening it would lift that refusal without a ruling (D-115, OQ-11 as built; D-163). TY 2025-26: the index \"notified ... under clause (v) of Explanation to section 48\" - the table of S.O. 1790(E) of 5-6-2017 (2001-02 = 100, ..., 2017-18 = 272) as amended by S.O. 2413(E) of 13-6-2018 (280), S.O. 3266(E) of 12-9-2019 (289), S.O. 1879(E) of 12-6-2020 (301), S.O. 2336(E) of 15-6-2021 (317), S.O. 2735(E) of 14-6-2022 (331), S.O. 2571(E) of 12-6-2023 (348), S.O. 2103(E) of 24-5-2024 (363) and S.O. 2954(E) of 1-7-2025 (376). TY 2026-27: the index \"notified ... under section 72(8)(a)\", 2026-27 \"384\" by S.O. 3889(E) of 15-7-2026, the earlier years carried over by 2025 Act s.536(2)(j). The table holds every year the divisor can ask for, because it is never taken before 2001-02 (2025 s.72(8)(b); 1961 s.48 Explanation (iii)). A year the table does not hold is refused. Every regime. Sources: docs/taxplanning-build/sources/2026-10-31-cost-inflation-index.md (six hashed Gazette copies) and 2026-09-28-perquisite-thresholds.md U1, T4, U2, T5.",
